  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support the MHPSS needs in Hatay</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of this program is to improve the health and well-being of refugees affected by the earthquakes. The proposed intervention serves as a provision for MHPSS services in Hatay T&#xfc;rkiye. The proposed area of intervention is Reyhanli, the sub-district of Hatay where SAMS is proposing a 12-month program to promote a long-term impact and reach beneficiaries given the crucial need for MHPSS services post the earthquake. Services will include specialized MHPSS consultations and free-of-charge psychotropic medications; individual psychotherapy sessions; group PSS activities; group awareness-raising sessions for caregivers related to PSS and protection concerns among children; and referrals to other services for clients, such as GBV case management and health services. During the project period, 2,220 direct beneficiaries will receive services.</narrative>
  </description>
